  "approved_requirements": "Read UTF-8 CSV with headers. Orders fields: product_id string, quantity decimal(18,2), city string. Prices fields: product_id string, price decimal(18,2). Require every listed field to be non-null, and string fields non-blank; require unique product_id in prices. On either validation failure stop without writing output. Finish both independent validations before joining. Inner join orders and prices on product_id; an order without a price is excluded. line_revenue = quantity * price; sum by city into revenue. Save Parquet to a new destination with errorifexists, never overwrite. Accept input/output paths as --orders, --prices, --output. Use explicit CSV schemas and stop SparkSession in finally. Test orders (A,2,Москва),(A,1,Москва),(B,3,Казань); prices (A,100),(B,50); expected Москва=300, Казань=150, irrespective of row order.",
